<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 12.55 bln levs 2-yr, floating notes.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 12.55 bln levs 2-yr, floating notes.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on Wednesday placed at par value a special issue of two-year, floater coupon T-notes worth 12.55 billion levs, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The coupon was set at two points over the BNB central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 14.15 percent monthly or 169.80 percent annually.</p>
<p>Coupon payments are due semi-annually and the principal will be redeemed at maturity, the central bank said in a statement. In line with its usual practice the central bank did not say with which financial intitution or institutions the issue was placed.</p>
<p>Details of issue follow. Price in percent of par.</p>
<p>Issue number		  BG2030097120</p>
<p> Type			    floater coupon</p>
<p> Term			    two years</p>
<p> Issue date		    April 16</p>
<p> Maturity date		 April 14, 1999</p>
<p> Par value		     12.55 bln levs</p>
<p> Selling price		 100 pct</p>
<p> Yield to maturity	   CIR+2 points</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
